    B -- Yes --> C{Condition Met?}
    C -- True --> D[Execute Block]
    D --> S1[Statement 1]
    D --> S2[Statement 2]
    D --> S3[...]
    D --> S4[Statement N]
    S4 --> E[Continue Program]
    C -- False --> E
    B -- No --> E
```

## Example from Class

The reference material frequently uses blocks within control flow statements. For instance, in the `demo_control_loops.c` file, the `if` and `else` statements each contain a block of code:

```c
