```
In the first `printf` line, `%c` is replaced by the value of the `section` variable (a character), and `%d` is replaced by the value of `super_mega_student_counter_3000` (an integer). In the second line, `%f` is replaced by the value of `averageScore` (a float).

## Explanation
Comments are special parts of your C code that are completely ignored by the compiler when your program is built. Their primary purpose is to provide human-readable explanations, notes, or documentation directly within the source code itself. This makes your code much easier for you and other programmers to understand, clarifying what specific sections of code do, why certain decisions were made, or to temporarily disable lines of code without deleting them.

